security-password command pages (x230): with the DUT in secure mode, set password requirements
(`security-password minimum-length`, `security-password minimum-categories`) and confirm every kind of user is held to them.
Procedure (pass criteria in brackets):
  1. new privilege-1 user: too short, then long but 1 category [both rejected], then compliant [accepted]
  2. new privilege-15 user: same three [rejected, rejected, accepted]
  3. existing users (the two just made, and `manager`): too short and 1-category passwords, with and without `privilege`
     [all rejected; stored hashes unchanged]
Not done: a console login as the new users with the compliant passwords. The console tools take another login only from the
CK_USER/CK_PASSWORD environment, and tools/tb does not carry environment over ssh.

