- The warning appears ONLY for the 20:16 secure-mode boot. The permanent log has none for tonight's earlier plain boots
  (18:0x-18:3x, run 1), and none after the 20:29 boot out of secure mode (below). The boot banner that time also said
  "Please verify release with the 'crypto verify' command".
- No `crypto verify <file> <hash>` pair is configured. Per the AW+ x230 `crypto verify` page, the hash is "the known correct
  checksum ... listed in the sha256sum file that is available from the Allied Telesis Download Center". This dev build
  (x230v2_28GS-awplus_main-20261008-57.rel) has no published sha256sum. The same page says "If the device is in Secure Mode
  and the boot-up firmware file fails verification [against a saved pair], the device will not boot". So `crypto verify`
  does not usefully apply to this dev build, and no pair was saved.
- The 08:48:07 line is the morning triage's read-only `show crypto secure-mode` (not a valid command), not tonight's run.

